So. Tammie the tourist made an offer to The Lady and a choir sang, and 
all that.

This was a straight-ahead game-- no bones files (none!), only one altar 
of any sort in the main dungeon (DL12), made the DSM the old-fashioned 
way from the first dragon that left scales (silver, but I already had a 
[SoR]). No Ludios. 

Grrl, my original pet, lasted until after Sokoban (BoH) but didn't, I 
think, make it through the Mines. I don't remember what got him, but by 
Minetown I had dwarvish mithril and a decent set of armor, and had 
reached basic proficiency with a long sword, so I'd pretty much gotten 
out of Grrl what I needed most. 

This PYEC deal is really fabulous. I loved knowing that I had enough 
charges on my /WoDeath, and being able to charge magic markers and 
/WoPolymorph. 

I spent a lot of time sacrificing on DL12, and got FireBrand, Mojo, 
Vorpy, a few spellbooks, and a bunch of glows. Protection points 7 and 8 
actually came directly from The Lady rather than from paying a priest. 
Since tourists can reach Basic in both long sword and hammer, I tried 
both out and found that I liked FireBrand better, so enchanted that up 
and planned to use it all the way through. 

But midway through Gehennom, there was FrostBrand sitting on the floor. 
I've used it before but even so I was still surprised at how much more 
effective FB is than FireBrand at equal enchantment.

Also in Gehennom, I reached XL 18 the hard way-- I assume I'd drunk a 
bl!GL in an attempt to get more manna and up my success rates with the 
Magic Mapping spell, but even so I don't remember the last time I 
leveled-up that high in melee. (And I finally wished for a Robe to make 
the spell do-able. Without it, I had a fail rate near 90% at best.)

Of course, the problem with FB, FireBrand, and Mojo is that potions 
evaporate. I noticed the lack of potions more in not having enough FH 
for my comfort level than in any deeply meaningful way, but before the 
final ascent I had something like 214 HP and 7 !FH to bring along, 
wasn't terribly comfortable with either aspect of that even though in a 
dozen ascensions I've never needed 7 !FH. (Okay, there was an A I lost 
on Astral that was outfought, but otherwise.) In any case, around 20 
more HP came from potions that showed up on the ascent.

The run to Rodney, to Moloch's, and back up was textbook aside from the 
fact that I'd forgotten that I needed to keep my blPYEC in my main 
inventory for MR. I realized the problem when my first malignant aura 
cursed my [GoP. A quick bl?RC and everything was fine, but still-- 
stupid.

The force pulled me back 10 times; Rodney showed up 4 times beyond the 
required viewings (DL39; DL24; DL17 double-trouble plus I'd forgotten to 
recharge my 0:1 /Death and the backups were all in my BoH in a sack, so 
I tried to outfight both of them--which didn't work terribly well--
before I got away long enough to get the PYEC and recharge; and DL5).

It was around DL5 on the way out that I realized that I'd forgotten my 
cache of K rations at the castle. Oh well, I'd have to do the planes 
with some food rations and a =SD, because I wasn't going back. 

Planes were standard; air was faster than usual. I got down to ~150 HP 
(out of ~230) but was never seriously threatened. On Astral, I planned 
to hit Death last to avoid the HP drain. So I went right first for 
Famine, TPed the crowds out of the way and found the chaotic altar. Came 
back and went left with Pestilence, TPed the gang again near the doorway 
to the altar room, heard a burp and felt sad for a moment about my pet 
Angel, Friend (awww), and offered. And a choir sang and all that.

Genociding L felt like a cop-out this time (and I didn't do it until the 
final run up-- I fought them just fine in Gehennom) but whatever, I 
survived.

Eleven classes down, Ra and H to go. 

